Foundry — Build-Verify-Fix Loop

Scope: self-target run
Spec: forge-specs/foundry-run-fallout/spec.md
Temper: enabled
Max Cycles: 5
UI: disabled

FOUNDRY_SCOPE=self-target run
FOUNDRY_SPEC=forge-specs/foundry-run-fallout/spec.md
FOUNDRY_URL=
FOUNDRY_TEMPER=true
FOUNDRY_NYQUIST=false
FOUNDRY_MAX_CYCLES=5
FOUNDRY_NO_UI=true
FOUNDRY_TICKET=
FOUNDRY_DESC=
FOUNDRY_SKIP_BACKEND=true
FOUNDRY_SERENA_HEALTH=HEALTHY

Use MCP tool Foundry-Init to create the run, then follow the phase guide.
Thread the invocation flags into that call: url=, temper=true, nyquist=false, max_cycles=5, no_ui=true
  — the FOUNDRY_URL, FOUNDRY_TEMPER, FOUNDRY_NYQUIST, FOUNDRY_MAX_CYCLES and FOUNDRY_NO_UI values above.
  max_cycles 0 is unbounded; reaching the cap ends the run in HALTED, which is NOT DONE.
  temper defaults off; a temper-off run still gets PROVE's adversarial half at INSPECT.
  no_ui declares that this run has no browsable UI, so the SIGHT browser audit is not part of it.
Call Foundry-Next at every step to get specific instructions.

Forge plans. Foundry builds.
